      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To investigate the effects of murine IL-12 (mIL-12) gene on the expression of CD44 and CD49d on pulmonary leukocytes."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL AND METHODS",
          "content": "BALB/c mice (n = 24) were sensitized to ovalbumin (OVA) by intraperitoneal injection and challenged with OVA aerosol for 7 consecutive days. mIL-12 plasmid was then intramuscularly administered in eight BALB/c mice every second day for three times during OVA challenge."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Administration of mIL-12 plasmid significantly reduced airway hyperreactivity, the expression of CD44 and CD49d on pulmonary leukocytes, pulmonary infiltration of inflammatory cells, Th2 cytokines production and goblet cell hyperplasia (P < 0.05). Importantly, the percentages of CD44+/CD49d+ leucocytes showed positive correlations with numbers of inflammatory cells, goblet cells hyperplasia and levels of IL-4 and IL-5 (P < 0.01)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Our study suggests that CD44 and CD49d might contribute to the preventive effects of mIL-12 gene in asthma."
        }
      ]},
